WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.820
- It's also Mother's Day this Sunday

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.849
so we wanna celebrate mama's.

00:00:04.849 --> 00:00:07.849
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.860
Mary, do your kids celebrate with you?

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.970
Do y'all do anything special?

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.340
- They do, but I'm a grandmother now

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.030
so part of what I'm
celebrating is my daughter Lily

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.520
who's just an amazing mother herself

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.180
and yeah, it's like the whole,

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.300
any excuse for our whole
gang to just pile in.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.831
Dogs, kids, babies, everybody.

00:00:29.831 --> 00:00:31.530
It's wonderful.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.363
- That is wonderful.

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:33.480
Especially as a grandma now.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.630
- Yeah, I love being a grandmother.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.980
It's so boring to say

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.450
but it is the greatest thing in the world.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.037
- I do too (audience laughing)

00:00:41.037 --> 00:00:42.090
- [Kelly] I know it's
special, it's different.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:46.560
- We text each other
grandmother photos all the time.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.120
- It's so, it must be so odd too.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.340
I have a six and eight
year old, but I can't

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.540
so obviously I can't imagine.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.120
But like to have your kids be mothers

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.953
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:56.853
Like, that's, that's interesting.

00:00:56.853 --> 00:00:57.810
That dynamic like being
like, wait, you're mom too.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.643
That's just weird.

00:00:58.643 --> 00:00:59.730
I can't look at my eight year old and go,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.699
I hope you do well. (laughing)

00:01:02.699 --> 00:01:03.690
Like, I hope I did well enough.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.523
What about y'all?

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:05.356
What do you do Diane?

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:06.189
- Leave me out. (laughing)

00:01:06.189 --> 00:01:07.022
- Leave me out.

00:01:07.022 --> 00:01:07.855
You're like, I don't wanna
celebrate Mother's day.

00:01:07.855 --> 00:01:08.688
- I'm just going to sit here.

00:01:08.688 --> 00:01:09.521
I'm enjoying it.(laughing)

00:01:09.521 --> 00:01:10.740
- Okay, well I gave you wine.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.573
I like this and

00:01:11.573 --> 00:01:12.420
- I'm glad I have this.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.954
- She's mildy inebriated.

00:01:13.954 --> 00:01:14.985
- [Kelly] I like this.

00:01:14.985 --> 00:01:17.430
- I'm sorry I can't share
with you everyone (laughing)

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.345
but I'm gonna drink up
right now. (laughing)

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.910
(audience cheering)

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.230
- [Kelly] We're gonna celebrate for you,

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.317
for Mother's day.

